course: dictionary
lesson: 5371
title: Kilometres and km
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Km is the short way to write kilometre, a unit for long distances. One km is 1000 metres. «The Thames is about 346 km long» means the river is about 346 thousand metres from end to end.
explain: Km/h means kilometres per hour, a unit of speed. It tells you how far something travels in one hour. «A car going 60 km/h» covers 60 kilometres every hour.
explain: In speech people often say «k» or «kay», as in «it's 5k to town» or «a 10k run». In formal writing the unit is often spelled out: «a distance of five kilometres». It is the same unit, just said or written in a different way.
fact: Km is short for kilometre, and 1 km is 1000 metres.
fact: Km/h is a speed: the number of kilometres travelled in one hour.
fact: «The Channel Tunnel is about 50 km long.»
fact: Australia, New Zealand, Canada and Ireland use km/h for speed limits; the USA and UK use miles.
fact: In casual talk the unit is often dropped, so «it's like 3 from here» means about 3 km.
exercise: What does km stand for? | *kilometre | kilogram | kilowatt | kilolitre
exercise: A car travels «60 km/h». How far does it go in one hour? | *60 kilometres | 600 kilometres | 60 metres | 6 kilometres
exercise: How many metres are in «1 km»? | 100 | 10000 | *1000 | 10
test: Which unit would best measure the distance between two towns? | grams | *kilometres | metres | litres
test: «The Mississippi system is about 6,000 km long.» How many metres is that? | *6,000,000 | 6,000 | 600 | 60,000
exam: Which best shows the speed of a train? | 120 m | 120 km | 120 kg | *120 km/h
